00:00.000  apparatus │ 
                      ── Plan: Combat basics
                      
00:00.000  apparatus │   ~ Walk somewhere dangerous, fight what lives there, and be paid for it. The oldest loop in the
                      genre, and the one that has to work before anything else is worth testing.
                      
                      It goes to the Sunken Crypt rather than the tavern, for two reasons. The crypt spawner keeps two
                      rats where Millbrook keeps one, and a library of plans that all queue for the same single mob is
                      a library that fails for reasons which have nothing to do with what it is testing. The second
                      reason is free: the way down is a zone boundary, so this also covers walking between zones,
                      which nothing else does.
                      
                      This plan was the one that found "a mob you are fighting can wander out of the room" — it used to
                      flag "waited for falls and never saw it", because the rat left one swing into the fight. Fixed;
                      the transcript now shows an exchange running its full length.
                      
                      The crypt below is the one fixture that builds *geography*: a zone, and two rooms dug down out of
                      the chapel. A room can only be created by digging it, because a room made from nothing has no
                      exit into it — so the passage and the room arrive together, which is how the builder does it too
                      (§7.6). The rats are sentinels, so unlike the hand-built world they are reliably standing there;
                      the wander-out-of-a-fight guard has its own coverage in the suite and does not need a plan to be
                      flaky to prove it.
