                      ── Wait for something to fight rather than assuming it is standing there. The crypt rats wander
                      between here and the ossuary, so the room is routinely empty on arrival — the first run of
                      this plan walked in, found nothing, and spent two minutes waiting for a fight it had never
                      started.
                      
                      This is as close to reliable as a plan against a live world gets: a rat can still wander out
                      between this line and the next. A plan that needs certainty needs to build its own mob, which
                      is what the world fixtures are for.
                      
